00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:28.260
<i>Say what to myself who gets excited easily?</i>

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.620
<i>Tomadou iibun</i>

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.620
<i>I'm confused, what to say</i>

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:40.840
<i>Dreamin' samenai yume ochiteku sadame</i>

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:40.840
<i>Dreamin' the never-waking dream,
the falling fate</i>

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:46.600
<i>Don't stop lovin' Can't stop lovin' U
Ya ya ya</i>

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:46.600
<i>Don't stop lovin' can't stop lovin' you
Ya ya ya</i>

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:55.950
<i>Believe in U hikikae ni subete ushinatte mo</i>

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:55.950
<i>I believe in you even if I lose everything for it</i>

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:01.480
<i>Still lovin' can't stop lovin' U
No no no</i>

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:01.480
<i>Still lovin' can't stop lovin' you
No no no</i>

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.090
<i>Tattoo Kiss</i>

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.090
<i>Tattoo Kiss</i>

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:13.440
That's right.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.230
This is my duel with fate!

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:21.440
Demon Spiral!

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:32.520
Her movements are too irregular;
it's impossible to follow.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:35.010
Amazing... Can he grab her?

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:42.060
Not good. She doesn't have enough height.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.320
A devil's maneuver?

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:10.130
That certainly might be appropriate
for a partner of mine.

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.520
Then...

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.390
It seems this has been decided.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:18.530
Amazing Angelic Counterattack

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:21.600
Amazing Angelic Counterattack

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:21.600
"Amazing Angelic Counterattack"

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.400
Amazing Angelic Counterattack

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.850
Even for someone like Sora,
it must be quite a shock this time.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.620
I can't even say anything to her.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.720
Let's leave her alone right now.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.150
Sora...

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.590
Demon Spiral...

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:48.760
May had a shoulder injury,

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.290
but she used that to invent a new maneuver.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:56.500
And she got the Phoenix Ticket.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.900
I...

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:03.310
Sora...

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.710
Miss Layla...

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:13.390
To tell you the truth, I didn't think
May would go that far either.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:17.090
I was actually moved by the fact
that she invented a new maneuver

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.430
by taking advantage of her injuries.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.830
I'm sorry.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:29.000
Three years ago, before Yuri and l
participated in the Circus Festival,

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.940
Kalos told us this:

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.410
Listen very carefully, both of you.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.280
If you cannot win, don't come back here.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:43.750
If you cannot win in the Circus Festival,
you two have nowhere to come back to.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:49.060
The Boss told you something like that?

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:53.600
That was why I didn't have
any choice but to win.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:59.090
But you won your duel with fate.
You really are amazing.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.530
What are you going to do now?

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:08.740
I will try to improve my skills so that
I can keep up with May.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:14.700
Sora, are you thinking you lost to May
because you didn't have enough skills?

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:16.120
What?

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.220
If I thought you didn't have enough skills,

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:22.620
I never would have recommended you.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:28.130
You lost because the festival meant
only that much to you. Am I right?

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:30.400
No, I never thought that way.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:35.700
To me, it was something I needed to
enter and win by all means.

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.540
To me, it was worth that much.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.640
But, for you, it was not worth that much.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.880
Sora, I will ask you one more time.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:50.180
Do you seriously want to participate in the
Circus Festival no matter what happens?

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:52.650
Yes!

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:57.860
Once you make up your mind and decide to
seriously follow through, you never give up.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:01.930
I know that better than anyone else.

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:07.700
But here you are, right now,
having given up on everything.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:10.360
That's proof that you weren't serious about it.

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:15.110
I think I told you after the Salome show.

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:20.050
I can't feel enough of that edge from you
right now to be scared of you.

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:22.740
You've lost track of what's important.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:29.660
I wanted you to enter to the festival.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.630
Miss Layla!

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.340
I can't believe what I did...

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.940
I...

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:54.380
I betrayed Miss Layla's expectations.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:03.490
Sora, Sora, take the tape off!

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:05.820
I want to do something. I have to do something.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:10.670
What can I do? Tell me, Fool!

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:13.070
I don't know the answer either.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:15.070
You're no help.

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.270
Aren't you supposed to be on my side?

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:20.010
Can't you give me some
clever advice or something?

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:24.780
I am the spirit of the stage.
I'm neither enemy nor ally.

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:28.820
One more time, I want to have one more chance.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:32.790
Oh, I can't believe I feel this way at this point.

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:35.290
I'm really pathetic.

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:36.890
The only thing I can tell you is this.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:42.190
The deadline for Circus Festival
entries hasn't passed yet.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:51.910
Sagittarius is still not able to
find its way out from the darkness.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:56.340
But, nearby Sagittarius,
I can see another arrow;

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.510
an arrow shining, as if it's guiding her
way out from the darkness.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.380
Another arrow?

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:06.840
Phoenix Tickets are the "seed" right
which were given to those two who won.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.560
Two...

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.290
Two!

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:16.090
There's one more ticket!

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.170
There is! There is! There is!

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:20.570
There's another ticket!

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:22.300
I can't breathe!

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:22.300
There's another ticket!

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:22.570
There's another ticket!

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:22.870
I'm gonna wee!

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:22.870
There's another ticket!

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:23.840
I'm gonna wee!

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:28.110
Yuri is studying in Paris right now, you know.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.610
The Circus Festival will be held in
Paris too. It's perfect!

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:33.480
Take me to Paris, quick!

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:34.520
Paris?

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.720
Yuri hasn't even registered for the festival!

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.420
He might not have any intention of being in it.

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:40.860
First of all, it's impossible to go to Paris by cab.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:43.660
Impossible or not, there's nothing to do but ask!

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:47.230
I realized that I can't just keep
moping about how I lost to May.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:52.000
I just have to acknowledge my defeat
and do what I can now.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:58.470
I'll end up being absent from Kids' Stage, but
Marion's accepted it, so things should be okay.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:01.040
Don't you think Sora's back to her usual self?

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.050
If it's true, we can't stop her now.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:05.510
Sora!

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:07.120
Rosetta!

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:10.250
This is the guide book for Paris which
I used to use a long time ago.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:13.220
There's a some French phrases too,
although it's not much.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:15.760
Thank you. This will help.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:19.730
Also, a winter coat. It's cold over there.

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:22.160
Rosetta, thank you.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:25.870
Bye!

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.370
Go, Sora!

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:30.740
Paris... It must be nice.

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:33.310
The clown I admire, Mr. Charlie is there.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:35.880
Oh! So Anna, you're rarin' to go too?

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:39.940
Well, if you put it like that, I'm PARIN' to go!

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:46.850
Je... Je...

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.450
Je t'aime.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:03.570
That's...

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:04.970
The God of Death, Leon!

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:07.340
The God of Death's come back.

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:14.620
I'll finish checking in.

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:16.450
Amazing.

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:20.220
Leon, I've not seen you for a long time.

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:21.890
Emma...

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:25.380
So you remember me? I'm glad.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:27.700
Are you his new partner?

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:32.030
That's right. I am Leon's partner, May Wong.

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:34.600
Poor you.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:38.470
Once the Circus Festival is over,
you'll be discarded too.

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:41.600
Hey! Just who are you?!

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.890
Hey, please don't put us on the
same floor as Leon.

00:10:50.890 --> 00:10:53.620
He'll make my performers nervous.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:55.460
If you can't arrange this, I'll change hotels!

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.650
Please wait for a moment...

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:01.730
There is a message for Mr. Ken Robbins
from Kaleido Stage.

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:03.590
What? For me?

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:09.540
"l will create a chance for you to show off."

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:12.670
So, did you hear it too?

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:14.610
The whisper of the God of Death?

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:19.700
I will create a perfect chance for you
to show off in today's show.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:26.280
"The whisper of the God of Death"?
Were you also Leon's partner?

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:32.730
Partner? Nobody can be Leon's partner.

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:35.060
Nobody but her.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:36.360
Her?

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:38.390
Sora's in Paris?

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:43.360
Er... The drama school where Yuri is...

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:47.680
I can't read French!

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:49.730
Where? Where? Where is he?

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:53.480
YURI!

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:09.000
I see. I'll try to look for her too.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:09.890
Goodbye.

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:15.930
Well, okay, but... where should I look?

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:20.000
Er... Me-Merci.

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:26.950
My money's all gone after l
took the cab. Well, but...

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:28.680
Yuri is here.

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:29.920
Non.

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:31.890
What? He is not here?

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:35.690
Mais, c'est bien ici le... Conservatoire...

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:39.090
Excuse... Oh, what shall I do...

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:41.700
If you're looking for Yuri,

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:44.070
he wasn't in class today.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:47.130
What? So, he is here, isn't he?

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:48.500
Yes.

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:49.500
You liar!

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:53.840
Excuse me, but do you know where Yuri is now?

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:56.410
He's, how should I put it, he
marches to his own beat,

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:59.210
or shall I say, he's difficult to approach...

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:01.020
But anyway, I don't really know.

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:02.550
Don't you know where he lives either?

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:03.620
Well...

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:04.820
Sorry.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:06.310
Bye.

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:10.820
So, there is no clue. What shall I do?

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:14.590
The Circus Festival...

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:15.960
I'm sure...

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:20.530
I'm sure Yuri will come here too.
I'm sure! I'm sure!

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:26.270
Oh... So, this is the hall.

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:29.000
Wow, they're performing! Oh...

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:33.140
Merci, merci.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:39.020
Oh, I know! If I make some money here,

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:42.190
I can look for Yuri, and I can eat something!

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:45.780
I'm not at a dead end yet. I'm not! I'm not!

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:51.400
Hey, they're getting fired up.

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:56.060
Oh, Mute and Alice.
She is something of a performer.

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:01.410
She's amazing. But I've never seen her before.

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:03.900
She's pretty good. Who is she?

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:10.510
Ta-da!

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:18.310
Huh?

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:20.260
Super!

00:14:20.260 --> 00:14:21.890
Brava!

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:27.130
Oh... Merci! Merci! Merci!

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.760
Wow, now I can eat something with this.

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:36.610
Hey, are you all right?

00:14:36.610 --> 00:14:38.580
Did you hurt yourself?

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:42.820
Oh... I understand what he is saying. I'm lucky.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:45.050
What?! What did you say? Hey!

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:58.970
Really... I thought you hurt yourself.
I was worried.

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:01.030
Whoever would have thought
she was just hungry?

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:05.410
I'm sorry! I haven't eaten anything
since I got to Paris, you see.

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:08.600
Then it's impressive that you can
manage maneuvers like that.

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:13.210
I wanted to enter the Circus Festival
no matter what, you see...

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:15.920
Are you going to participate in the festival?

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:17.320
I want to!

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.290
Mute and Alice, you too?

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:20.290
Yeah.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:24.990
We want to win in the festival and
get the world's attention,

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:29.660
and organize a performance team with
these guys right here, and travel around.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.330
That is our dream.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:35.640
Everyone's dreams rest
heavily on Mute's shoulders.

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:37.140
Well, I guess.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:39.730
Wow!

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:44.010
Didn't you also come here to make
your dream come true, Sora?

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:47.350
Don't give up that dream.

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:51.120
An angel always keeps an eye
on us somewhere.

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:53.090
An angel...

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:55.560
My angel...

00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:58.760
Sora!

00:15:58.760 --> 00:15:59.820
Yes!

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:01.060
Huh?

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:05.370
What do you know, it's Sora.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:07.270
Yuri!

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:10.000
Yuri... Don't tell me he's THE Yuri Killian.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:12.970
Does she know Yuri Killian
who won the last time?

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:14.940
Who on Earth is she?

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.710
Yuri!

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:20.210
Oh, I'm glad. I finally found you.

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:24.020
I was sure you would come here.

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:26.620
Whoever thought I would see you
in a place like this?

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:28.260
It's been a long time, hasn't it?

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:29.890
Yes!

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:32.730
An angel always keeps an eye on you.

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:38.030
Miss Layla, I will never give up on
participating in this Circus Festival.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:46.740
Hmm... It's such a different atmosphere
from America or Japan.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:48.580
It's calm, isn't it?

00:16:48.580 --> 00:16:50.040
Yes.

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:52.840
It looks like you've completely adjusted to Paris.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:55.350
You think so?

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:56.680
Yes.

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:05.230
Well... To tell you the truth,

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:10.000
I came to Paris because
I wanted to ask you a favor.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.900
A favor? What kind?

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:17.040
You have Phoenix Tickets, don't you?

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:18.910
Yes, I do. Why?

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:20.670
Using those tickets,

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:24.450
I want you to participate in the
Circus Festival with me.

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:26.810
That is a big favor.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:32.750
Please, Yuri! You're the only hope left for me!

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:39.290
Sora, I didn't happen to be there
just by coincidence.

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:42.760
I went there looking for you
after Layla asked me.

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:45.400
What? Miss Layla?

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:50.440
And I've heard the gist of
what happened at Kaleido Stage.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.340
Then...

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:56.300
But I think this is too tough for you.

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:00.340
Why?

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:08.560
Sora, you really don't know
what kind of place this festival is.

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:11.620
This is the place that can
make your dreams come true.

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:16.200
But at the same time, it's also a place
where you destroy the dreams of others.

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.630
I already know that.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:24.310
And I also know that victory means
beating everybody else.

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:28.910
But, I have to win here.

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:33.450
Here, there's no such thing as fair play,
friendship, or consideration.

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:37.020
If you let your guard down, someone
will get the jump on you.

00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:39.720
Do you know this is that kind of world?

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.950
Yes, I do.

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:45.430
Then, for example, if a friend of yours,

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.230
Let's say Ken,

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:50.360
suddenly collapsed just before you perform,

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:55.470
and you received a call saying that he was
in the hospital and wanting to see you...

00:18:55.470 --> 00:18:57.800
What would you do?

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:01.380
At that time...

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:06.050
It's possible that the call was
a lie made up by another performer.

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:08.480
Yes, that's true...

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:13.020
Sorry. I think that question was a little mean.

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:14.280
All right.

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:16.990
Yuri...

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:20.950
Let's participate in the festival together.
I will submit an entry application tomorrow.

00:19:21.830 --> 00:19:23.760
Thank you!

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:30.000
So this is where you live.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.970
Wow... Did you paint all these, Yuri?

00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:35.140
Yeah.

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:37.310
What with spending all my time commuting
back and forth between here and school,

00:19:37.310 --> 00:19:39.480
maybe I started wanting some company.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:43.380
I just casually picked up a brush,
and then I was completely into it.

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:46.350
Everyone is smiling.

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.920
When I was at Kaleido Stage,

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:52.190
I don't think I looked at
the audience's faces much.

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:57.500
When I started painting,

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:02.130
I realized how wonderful smiling faces were.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:05.370
Is this the picture you're painting now?

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:10.110
Yeah. When I tried to capture the essence
of the smile, it became an angel.

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:13.540
Angel...

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:29.460
It's May. I'd like to start training soon,
if that's all right.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:30.930
All right.

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:34.930
So, this is it.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:39.570
Leon Oswald, eh?

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:42.780
In order to beat Leon and May's Demon Spiral,

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:46.440
I suppose we need a maneuver on par with it?

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:50.050
Shall we try an angel's maneuver?

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:52.590
An angel's maneuver?

00:20:52.590 --> 00:20:56.680
That's right. To counter their demon maneuver.

00:20:57.490 --> 00:20:58.930
Yes.

00:20:58.930 --> 00:21:00.530
Sora?

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:02.530
We will help your practice.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:04.500
Mute and Alice?

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:07.130
It must be hard because you don't
have too much time.

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:11.760
And we also can learn something if we get
to watch the previous winner's practice.

00:21:12.510 --> 00:21:13.840
What do you want to do, Sora?

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:17.080
Since they offered us a hand, I think
we should accept their offer.

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:18.110
That's what she says.

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:19.150
Thank you.

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:20.340
I'm glad.

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:23.150
Even among those people who enter the festival,

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:26.480
there are nice people like Mute and Alice.

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:30.720
Good! Then, go higher like that!

00:21:31.630 --> 00:21:33.530
No! Not good at all.

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:36.090
Okay!

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:42.190
Do it like you're flying upwards
on your own power!

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:43.860
Yes!

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:51.370
I won't lose to May! I'll definitely win!

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:54.250
In order to meet Miss Layla's expectations.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:57.380
Demon Spiral!

00:22:02.190 --> 00:22:04.060
That speed is your limit?

00:22:04.060 --> 00:22:05.160
No! I can go faster!

00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:07.430
Then speed up to your limit!

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:08.220
Yes!

00:22:09.030 --> 00:22:13.770
That's right. Do it more slowly.
Like an angel's wings...

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:14.670
Yes!

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:18.600
So, this is a winning candidate's maneuver...

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:25.450
I'm going to win no matter what!

00:22:25.450 --> 00:22:27.050
The one to win will be...

00:22:27.050 --> 00:22:28.780
me!

00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:35.290
<i>Sekasu you ni muragaru Hard luck</i>

00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:35.290
<i>All kinds of hard luck flocks your way
as if it's spurring you on</i>

